                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Somewhere between [i]Roadworks Simulator 2016[/i] and literally any zombie horde rush game released in the past ten years lies [b]XCavalypse[/b] which, despite its initial problems, deserves all the credit in the world for actually finding something to do with the walking corpse genre that hasn't already been rehashed to death and back.\n\nGluing you into the cockpit of a six ton digging machine, your sole aim is to use the boom and bucket to swat, dismember and decapitate the waves of living dead that stagger towards you. There's currently three arcade-style game modes to pick from (Clean Up, Survival and Head Pop which are, disappointingly, exactly the same thing), as well as a tutorial which seems to be the introductory chapter to a campaign mode, voice acting and all.\n\nThe biggest issue here is that the excavator itself is an absolute hippo to control. I think it might actually be easier to attempt to drive one in real life. I used to live next door to a simpleton that owned one and he deserved a round of applause every time he managed to make a bowl of cereal without eviscerating himself so I find it hard to fathom that pushing this thing around the map should be such an ordeal. Attempting legitimate simulation is fair enough but I found it at odds with [b]XCavalypse[/b]'s bright arcade aesthetics. Even trying to get the damn thing to roll in a straight line without the bucket trying to pick its own wheels off is a fruitless nightmare.\n\nI like the skeleton of what's being attempted here though. Simplify and multiply should be the final release strategy; maybe knock a bulldozer or a combine harvester into the mix and you'd have yourself a winner.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VNdPmnuXMQU",
